---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import { CLIENTS } from '../data/site';
---

<Marketing
  title="Clients — Concord"
  description="Armada, Vector, and Accordion are independent applications that speak the Concord protocol. A community created in one opens in the others."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-hairline">
    <div class="cx-radial pointer-events-none absolute inset-0"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
      <p class="cx-eyebrow">Clients</p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-balance text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl"
      >
        Three independent apps. One protocol.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-300">
        Concord has no reference client and no blessed implementation. These are
        separate teams building separate applications against the same
        specification — which is exactly the property that makes the protocol
        worth anything.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
        A community created in one client opens in the others. Your identity is a
        key rather than an account, so it travels with you, and if a client ever
        disappoints you the community does not go with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
      <div class="space-y-6">
        {
          CLIENTS.map((client, index) => (
            <article class="cx-card overflow-hidden">
              <div class="grid gap-8 p-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-start lg:gap-16 lg:p-10">
                <div>
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-600">
                      0{index + 1}
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">
                      {client.name}
                    </h2>
                    <span class="rounded-md border border-hairline px-2 py-1 font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400">
                      {client.author}
                    </span>
                  </div>

                  <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-mint">
                    {client.tagline}
                  </p>

                  <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-300">
                    {client.description}
                  </p>

                  <ul class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                    {client.platforms.map((platform) => (
                      <li class="rounded-md border border-hairline bg-raised px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-gray-400">
                        {platform}
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="flex shrink-0 flex-col gap-2.5 lg:w-56">
                  {client.links.map((link, linkIndex) => (
                    <a
                      href={link.href}
                      rel="noopener"
                      class:list={[
                        'cx-btn w-full',
                        linkIndex === 0 ? 'cx-btn-primary' : 'cx-btn-ghost',
                      ]}
                    >
                      {link.label}
                    </a>
                  ))}
                  <a
                    href={client.source}
                    rel="noopener"
                    class="mt-1 text-center text-sm text-gray-500 transition-colors hover:text-mint"
                  >
                    View source
                  </a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="cx-eyebrow">Choosing</p>
          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-balance text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl"
          >
            They are not the same product.
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
            <p>
              <span class="text-gray-100">Armada</span> is the one to pick if you
              are replacing Discord outright. It has the full feature surface —
              threads, voice and video, custom emoji and themes, a Discord bridge
              and server import — and it speaks other community protocols
              alongside Concord.
            </p>
            <p>
              <span class="text-gray-100">Vector</span> is the one to pick if
              privacy is the requirement rather than the feature. It is a native
              application built around encrypted local storage and an optional
              Tor transport, from the team that co-authored the specification.
            </p>
            <p>
              <span class="text-gray-100">Accordion</span> is the one to read if
              you are implementing Concord yourself. It runs entirely in the
              browser with no backend, and it demonstrates how little code the
              protocol actually requires.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="cx-eyebrow">Interoperability</p>
          <h2
            class="mt-4 text-balance text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl"
          >
            What travels between them.
          </h2>
          <dl class="mt-6 divide-y divide-hairline border-y border-hairline">
            <div class="py-4">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-100">Your identity</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
                One key logs you in everywhere, across Concord clients and the
                wider Nostr ecosystem.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="py-4">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-100">
                Your memberships
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
                The Community List syncs across your devices and across clients —
                two different apps can serve one identity.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="py-4">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-100">Invite links</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
                An invite minted by one client opens in another. The base domain
                is interchangeable; only the locator and fragment are protocol.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="py-4">
              <dt class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-100">
                The community itself
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-400">
                Roles, channels, bans, and pins are Control Plane state that every
                client folds identically. There is no per-client interpretation.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <a
            href="/build/"
            class="mt-8 inline-flex text-sm text-mint transition-opacity hover:opacity-80"
          >
            Build a fourth client &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
